  "note": "Cbt Gp option 1: the area divided into sectors by the mission, the task and the number of BGs; the heavy BG on the most likely approach where the En main armour threat is expected, the second BG against the En secondary effort, the third in reserve for other eventualities or to reinforce (p 16 para 28 a (1)). Concept and Conduct of SZ Battle (C&SC handout, SZB): a Cbt Gp is an all-arms group on an Armd or Mech Bde HQ, armour heavy with at least two Armr Regts or mech heavy with at least two MIBs (p 5 para 9 g); for the C Tps an Armd Bde with 1-2 HAT Bns, or a Mech Bde with a HAT Bn and an Armr Regt (p 12 para 23 a). The SZ is divided into sectors, a BG to each (p 4 para 9 a); a Cbt Gp on 60-70 km (p 13 para 24 a). The options assume air, arty and AD support (p 16 para 28). The DLs 9 km apart, the BHOL 6 km behind the last DL, a BG's posn 3 km deep: a decision (E: the handout draws no scale).",
